@1010 = ~Evergreen Lance +3~
@1011 = ~The Evergreen Lance was originally designed to protect against outerplanar creature through an intense connection with the Prime Material Plane. Despite this lofty goal, the connection has faded through the ages as it has instead become a prized weapon in the endless and bloody succession fights of druidic orders across Faerûn. Tired of the endless disputes over the Evergreen Lance, the javelin was finally removed from the druidic infighting and reprisals by the Grand Druid herself. She demanded the lance as a tribute from one of her Archdruids, and then promptly fenced it so that none of the druids could trace the item.

While the power has faded, the Evergreen Lance still retains some of its power to fight outerplanar creatures. 

STATISTICS:

Combat abilities:
– Returns to the wielder's hand when thrown
– Double damage vs. outerplanar creatures
– 5% chance of quadruple damage vs. outerplanar creatures instead of double

THAC0: +3
Damage: 1d%melee_die%+3 (melee, piercing)
Damage: 1d%ranged_die%+3 (thrown, missile)
Speed Factor: 1
Proficiency Type: Spear
Type: One-handed
Requires:
 5 Strength

Weight: 2~
@1012 = ~Evergreen Lance +4~
@1013 = ~The Evergreen Lance was originally designed to protect against outerplanar creature through an intense connection with the Prime Material Plane. Despite this lofty goal, the connection has faded through the ages as it has instead become a prized weapon in the endless and bloody succession fights of druidic orders across Faerûn. Tired of the endless disputes over the Evergreen Lance, the javelin was finally removed from the druidic infighting and reprisals by the Grand Druid herself. She demanded the lance as a tribute from one of her Archdruids, and then promptly fenced it so that none of the druids could trace the item.

You have managed to unlock more of the Evergreen Lance's power to fight outerplanar creatures. 

STATISTICS:

