@1016 = ~The Iron Elegy~
@1017 = ~Javelins are typically light, flexible spears designed primarily as a throwing weapon. However the Iron Elegy weghs heavy in your hands due to its iron shaft and steel tip. 

Mubark was a half-ogre who dwelled near the Forest of Tethir. After a dispute with a local cleric who tried to drive Mubark from the land, Mubark commissioned the Elegy to counter the cleric's magic and was able to defend his home from further incursions.

STATISTICS:

Combat abilities:
– Returns to the wielder's hand when thrown
– 10% chance that target is silenced for two rounds (Save vs. Spell negates)

THAC0: +2
Damage: 1d%ranged_die%+2 (thrown, missile)
Damage: 1d%melee_die%+2 (melee, piercing)
Speed Factor: 2
Proficiency Type: Spear
Type: One-handed
Requires:
 12 Strength

Weight: 15~
@1018 = ~Silence~
@1019 = ~Javelin of Fire~
@1020 = ~Javelins are light, flexible spears designed primarily as a throwing weapon. They are usually constructed of wood and tipped with a small metal spearhead. The shaft is much thinner than a two-handed spear. The javelin is a ranged weapon, intended to be thrown. While javelins can be used for melee combat, they are not sturdy enough and perform poorly.

The javelin of fire is a magical javelin that will burst into flames as it is fired at an enemy. The effect is similar to a javelin doused in oil and set to flame.

STATISTICS:

Combat abilities:
– Hit target must save vs. Spell or suffer 1d4 points of fire damage

THAC0: +1
Damage: 1d%ranged_die%+1 (thrown, missile)
Damage: 1d%melee_die%+1 (melee, piercing)
Speed Factor: 3
Proficiency Type: Spear
Type: One-handed
Requires:
 5 Strength

Weight: 2~
// cespenar's dialogue for the evergreen upgrade
@1021 = ~Ooooh. Oh. Uh. Boss you nots mad at Cepsnar right? This Evergreen Lance gets extra pointy for imps!~
@1022 = ~And it could gets more pointy with two emeralds, but I don't see the right shinies here. I guess I keeps looking.~
@1023 = ~With two emerald shinies it gets more pointy! For 10,000 gp, you wants?~
@1024 = ~Oh well, Cespenar likes his Evergreen dull and unpointy.~


// why the jump in numbers? this was originally written for G3CIP and I didn't want to re-index
@1073 = ~Aye, now this is a turn. The Evergreen Lance. There was trouble out near Trademeet, and several druids went looking for this.~
@1074 = ~I can feel a power, but its faded since it's been idle too long. A pair of emeralds should do the trick.~
@1075 = ~Oh, and ye have some emeralds as well. We can use those to improve the Evergreen even further.~
@1076 = ~It'll cost ye 5,000 gold and without me apprentice, you'll need to stay on a day and help me run the forge.~
@1077 = ~What would that take?~
@1078 = ~No, I'm not interested. Is there anything else you can use?~
@1079 = ~No, I don't think so. I think I'll be going now.~
@1080 = ~Yes, let's do it.~
@1081 = ~Well, let's see what ye've got then.~